    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d888">

                <pb facs="0770" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48/3448a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-06">April 6, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>632. For Wayne Taylor<anchor n="17" xml:id="d888-f1"/> from American Red Cross:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“As we urgently require permission to continue our shipments of medical
                            supplies and clothing to meet the desperate needs in Poland suggest you
                            endeavor secure extension present arrangement with blockade authorities
                            without awaiting decision as to foodstuffs. Quantities our supplies,
                            including innumerable articles of clothing produced by volunteers
                            throughout country, are now awaiting shipment and further delays would
                            result in great embarrassment. Gratified to know that Johnson and you
                            are proceeding through foreign office. Davis 393”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d888-f1" n="17" xml:id="d888-f1-content">
                <p>Wayne Chatfield Taylor, American Red Cross Delegate in Paris.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
